  "analysis": [
    {
      "label": "Context",
      "text": "Stoppage time on the opening night of the Friends Arena, with Sweden 3–2 up. Ibrahimović had scored all three Swedish goals, and England still had bodies pushed up, leaving room behind their back line."
    },
    {
      "label": "Key moment",
      "text": "The long ball sent Hart sprinting well outside the area. The keeper got there first but could only head it high and short, straight to Ibrahimović, around 30 metres out with the goal unguarded."
    },
    {
      "label": "The technique",
      "text": "The ball was dropping over Ibrahimović's shoulder with back to goal, so a bicycle kick was the only way to strike it first time. Leaning back and meeting it high, the striker sent it looping over the retreating defenders."
    },
    {
      "label": "The finish",
      "text": "With Hart stranded, the shot needed height and accuracy rather than power. It came down short of the line and ran on into the empty net, completing Ibrahimović's four-goal night."
    }
  ],
